# T-1538: New named-key constructor syntax [type CtorName: [field: Type] ...]
# Named entries with uppercase keys declare payload constructors.
# Positional bare uppercase words declare unit constructors.
# Mixed forms are valid: [type File: [path: String] Noop]
[
  Result: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
  ok-val:  [Result.Ok value: 42]
  err-val: [Result.Error msg: "fail"]
  ok-matched: [match [Result.Ok value: 1]
    [case [let v] [Result.Ok v]    v.value]
    [Result.Error _]:              0]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(value), "Error": Function(msg)}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(42)})), "err-val": Variant(Result.Error, Dict({"msg": String("fail")})), "ok-matched": Int(1)})
